        "Screening test, fully worked. Prevalence 0.01, sensitivity 0.95, so true positives contribute 0.0095. Specificity 0.98, so false positives contribute 0.99 times 0.02, which is 0.0198. A positive result therefore has 0.0095 over 0.0293, about 0.324, chance of being genuine. The surprise is the base rate at work: even a 95 percent sensitive test misses most cases when the condition is rare, which is why confirmation follows screening.",
        "Tree diagram for two draws without replacement from 5 red and 3 blue. First red: 5 over 8. Then second red: 4 over 7, because one red is gone. Multiply along the red-red path: 5 over 8 times 4 over 7 equals 20 over 56, which is 5 over 14, about 0.357. The branches make the changing denominators visible, preventing the common mistake of reusing 5 over 8 on the second draw.",
