        "Treating a quota or convenience sample as random voids every formula in this section, because the standard error assumes known, positive selection probabilities. Calling 200 friendly passers-by a random sample and attaching plus or minus 7 percent to the result is precisely the malpractice this section exists to unmask. Randomness is a property of the selection procedure, not of the sample's appearance.",
