        "Polling organisations report support as 52 percent with a margin of 3 points, that is, the interval 49 to 55 percent at 95 percent confidence. A lead inside the combined margins is not a decisive lead. Editors who headline two-point gaps inside a 3-point margin commit the exact misreading this section exists to prevent, and careful analysts answer with the interval, not the point.",
        "Acceptance sampling in industry uses intervals on the mean fill or mean tensile strength: a batch passes when the 95 percent interval for its mean lies wholly inside specification limits. This turns quality decisions into interval statements rather than single-number gambles, and it lets a plant choose sample size in advance to meet a required decision precision.",
