        "Project data arrive dirty: duplicate submissions, skipped questions, impossible values, mixed codes for missing answers. The codebook defines every variable, its allowed range and its missing code; the cleaning log records each fix, dated. Validation at entry, such as rejecting ages above 100, prevents half the damage. A {S} project that cannot show its codebook and log cannot show where its numbers came from, and examiners notice.",
